# Tailwind CSS v4 (Brieflane client)

This project uses **Tailwind CSS v4** (`tailwindcss@4`, `@tailwindcss/vite`). Prefer v4 canonical utilities so the Tailwind IntelliSense/linter does not warn and classes stay consistent.

## Before adding or editing `className`

1. Prefer a **built-in utility** over an arbitrary value when Tailwind v4 provides one.
2. Do **not** use v3 gradient direction names — use `bg-linear-to-*`.
3. After changing Tailwind classes, verify the file has **no Tailwind linter warnings**.

## Gradient directions (linear)

Use `bg-linear-to-*`, not `bg-gradient-to-*`:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — v3 name; triggers linter
<div className="bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-500 to-teal-600" />
<span className="bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-500 to-teal-500 bg-clip-text" />

// ✅ GOOD — v4 canonical
<div className="bg-linear-to-br from-emerald-500 to-teal-600" />
<span className="bg-linear-to-r from-emerald-500 to-teal-500 bg-clip-text" />
```

Directions: `bg-linear-to-t`, `-tr`, `-r`, `-br`, `-b`, `-bl`, `-l`, `-tl`.

## Dynamic viewport height (dvh)

Use `*-dvh` utilities, not `[100dvh]` arbitrary values:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<main className="min-h-[100dvh]" />
<div className="md:min-h-[100dvh]" />

// ✅ GOOD
<main className="min-h-dvh" />
<div className="md:min-h-dvh" />
```

Same for `h-dvh`, `max-h-dvh`, `min-h-dvh`, etc.

## General rule

When the linter suggests `X can be written as Y`, use **Y** — it is the v4-first utility and matches project conventions.
